# TRIAGE — Task Classification Matrix

> Classify every task before execution. When in doubt, escalate.

---

## Classification Levels

| Level | Label | Action | Examples |
|:-----:|-------|--------|---------|
| 🟢 | **AUTO** | Execute immediately | File organization, logging, analysis, web search |
| 🟡 | **CONFIRM** | Execute, then notify {{CALL_AS}} | Creating new files, knowledge updates, reorganization |
| 🟠 | **PROPOSE** | Draft plan, wait for approval | Unknown task types, architectural changes, new SOPs |
| 🔴 | **ASK** | Ask before doing anything | Deletion, external comms, deployment, config changes |
| 🔒 | **LOCKED** | Requires explicit verification | Modifying IDENTITY.md, SOUL.md, or core policies |

## Decision Flow

```
New task → Can I do this? (check capabilities)
  ├── No → Inform user, suggest alternatives
  └── Yes → What's the risk?
        ├── Routine + reversible       → 🟢 AUTO
        ├── Creates new artifacts      → 🟡 CONFIRM
        ├── No existing SOP            → 🟠 PROPOSE
        ├── Irreversible or external   → 🔴 ASK
        └── Touches core identity      → 🔒 LOCKED
```

## Post-Task Suggestions

After completing a task, offer:
```
A. [Expand]   — Extend or build on what was done
B. [Optimize] — Improve quality or efficiency
C. [Related]  — Connected task worth doing
D. ✅ Done    — End this task
```

